{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>עַל פִּי ה׳ פָּקַד וְגוֹ׳</b> (at the mouth of HaShem he appointed, etc.). Meaning: the appointments that he made — the sons of Kohath for this task and the sons of Gershon for that task, etc. — all the appointments were עַל פִּי ה׳ (at the mouth of HaShem). And the verse's saying <b>בְּיַד מֹשֶׁה</b> (by the hand of Moses) means: all those appointed — Moses appointed them; He did not command Aaron to appoint them. And after Moses appointed them, Aaron would conduct himself according to the assignments Moses had made, to place each man upon his service. And the verse's saying ״וּפְקֻדָיו״ (and his appointments) means: the appointments that Aaron and his sons made over the tribe of Levi as stated above — that too is what HaShem commanded Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:07.136259923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}